Class demo::T { id: String[1]; v: Float[0..1]; }

###Relational
Database demo::DB ( Table T (ID VARCHAR(20) PRIMARY KEY, V REAL) )

###Mapping
Mapping demo::M
( demo::T: Relational { ~primaryKey ([demo::DB]T.ID) ~mainTable [demo::DB] T
    id: [demo::DB]T.ID, v: [demo::DB]T.V } )

###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection demo::Conn
{ store: demo::DB; type: DuckDB; specification: DuckDB { }; auth: Test; }
###Runtime
Runtime demo::RT { mappings: [ demo::M ]; connections: [ demo::DB: [ env: demo::Conn ] ]; }

###Data
Data demo::Seed { Relational #{ default.T: 'ID,V\n' + 'R1,3.5\n'; }# }

###Service
Service demo::Tre
{
  pattern: '/tre';
  documentation: 'Round-trip of SQL REAL as Pure Float. Grammar and compiler accept a type; whether the CONNECTOR can convert it is a separate question and is what this asks.';
  execution: Single
  {
    query: |demo::T.all()->project(~[id:x|$x.id, v:x|$x.v]);
    mapping: demo::M; runtime: demo::RT;
  }
  testSuites: [ s: { data: [ connections: [ env: Reference #{ demo::Seed }# ] ]
    tests: [ t: { serializationFormat: PURE_TDSOBJECT; asserts: [ a: EqualToJson
      #{ expected: ExternalFormat #{ contentType: 'application/json'; data: '[]'; }#; }# ] } ] } ]
}
